# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Nod runtime data (DEPLOYMENT §2: NOD_TRACE_DIR, NOD_DB_PATH)
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# The Track A corpus is committed, deliberately and directly, not via LFS
# (ROADMAP Phase 1). `say` is macOS-only and there is no cross-platform way to
# regenerate the seed, so committing the audio is the only route to a bench that
# runs on a clean clone. `source/` is committed too: it holds the sliced source
# clips and their manifest, which is what lets `corpus.build` rebuild the corpus
# on a machine without macOS.
!data/corpus/

# The Track C **scripts** are committed; the recordings are not yet a decision.
# `data/*` had hidden them entirely: script A was written at Gate 8 and has never
# been in git, so a clone had no scripts at all and the recording session — the
# one artifact in this project that cannot be regenerated — depended on files
# that existed on exactly one machine. They are 13 small JSON files.
# The audio is a separate call, taken when it exists: Track A's precedent
# (ROADMAP Phase 1, ~38 MB committed directly) argues for committing it, and the
# consent line in TRACK_C_SCRIPT §8 says the reader must agree to MIT-licensed
# audio in a public repository before that happens.
!data/trackC/
!data/trackC/scripts/
data/trackC/*.wav
.nodcache/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Bench output; committed traces under bench/traces/ are the exception (BENCH_SPEC §7)
bench/runs/*
!bench/runs/.gitkeep
# **Live artifacts are committed, simulated ones are not**, and the asymmetry is
# INV-9's. The simulated table is regenerated by `make bench` on a clean clone in
# seconds, so committing it would be a second copy of a derivable thing. A live
# table cannot be regenerated without spending credits against an account nobody
# else has, and it is the *provenance* for every number in README.md and
# docs/RESULTS.md — `test_readme_table_region_is_machine_owned` checks the README
# region against exactly this file, so ignoring it would make the check
# unrunnable on a clean clone the moment Phase 4 publishes. DEPLOYMENT §9 already
# asks for "docs/RESULTS.md regenerated, traces committed"; this is that.
!bench/runs/*.live.*
bench/report.html

# Secrets (INV-5). .env.example is committed, .env never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Console (P8)
node_modules/
.next/
out/

# OS
.DS_Store

# `make gate` scratch log
.gate.log

# hypothesis example database; a local cache of falsifying examples
.hypothesis/
.gate.ok

# /brag scratch output. Generated, timestamped, never committed.
brag-output-*/
brag-output/

# Demo-video voiceover renders. Regenerable from docs/VIDEO_SCRIPT.md via
# `hyperframes tts --voice af_heart`; 21 MB of WAV does not belong in git.
video-vo-*/
